{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3429","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3429","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3429\",\"parent_revision\":\"249513c93c604d4e324c8b392641e3e2a3124f1137b7be9a5b213742a07a1ab3\",\"root_revision\":\"249513c93c604d4e324c8b392641e3e2a3124f1137b7be9a5b213742a07a1ab3\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nTen plugin-creator SKILL.md files reference a shared doc as a backticked path instead of a markdown link. That is a workaround for an upstream skilllint bug, not a preference, and it should be reverted when the bug is fixed.\\n\\nCurrent form in the 10 files:\\n\\n    `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/docs/runtime-environment.md` \u2014 contains <what>; read before <when>.\\n\\nTarget form once unblocked:\\n\\n    [runtime-environment.md](${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/docs/runtime-environment.md) \u2014 contains <what>; read before <when>.\\n\\nImpact if this stands: the repo's own reference convention (`rules/markdown-file-references.md`, \\\"use a markdown link for any real relative path\\\") is contradicted in ten files by a workaround whose cause is invisible at the call site. New skills will copy the backtick form as if it were the convention, and the exception outlives the bug.\\n\\nUPSTREAM CAUSE \u2014 skilllint LK001 false positive on relative invocation.\\nskilllint does expand the variable; `packages/skilllint/rules/lk_series.py` lists `CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT` and `CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR` in `_STATICALLY_RESOLVABLE_CLAUDE_VARS`. The defect is the join afterwards: `check_lk001` computes `(skill_dir / resolved_url).resolve()`, and on a relative invocation `find_plugin_dir` returns a relative root, so the plugin path is appended to the skill path rather than replacing it. Measured on `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/component-patterns`, identical content: relative invocation reports 2 LK001 findings, absolute reports 0. Pre-commit passes relative paths, so it fires on every commit.\\n\\nReported to the skilllint maintainer session on 2026-09-06 with the reproduction, the suggested fix at the substitution site (`lk_series.py` ~178-186, return absolute substitutions), and a note that `test_internal_link_validator.py` appears to use absolute fixtures only, which is why it passes today.\\n\\nTRIGGER: a skilllint release whose LK001 resolves `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` link targets correctly under a relative invocation.\\n\\nVERIFY BEFORE REVERTING:\\n\\n    uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/plugin-creator/skills/component-patterns\\n\\nZero LK001 findings from that *relative* invocation means the bug is fixed. It already returns zero when given an absolute path, so an absolute check proves nothing.\\n\\nTHEN:\\n1. Convert the backticked form back to a markdown link in the 10 files (`git grep -l 'CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/docs/runtime-environment.md' -- plugins/plugin-creator/skills`).\\n2. Trim the workaround paragraph from the substituted-paths exception in `rules/markdown-file-references.md`, keeping the rule that the variables substitute and that the annotation contract is preserved.\\n3. Re-run pre-commit to confirm skilllint passes on the link form.\\n\\nOUT OF SCOPE \u2014 do not conflate. Six plugin-creator agents state the three-part test inline with no path at all. That is a separate decision driven by substitution in agent bodies being undocumented and unverified, not by this skilllint bug. Fixing skilllint does not license adding `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` back into agent prose; that needs its own canary test first (`rules/skill-substitution.md` names `/example-argument-substitution`).\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session melodic-plotting-emerson (2026-09-06), PR #3427\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"cb90c4c4c297cd6d7989daa8ad5619270279b027422d6f4bf86fafb42f78ef1b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSzTMYA\"}"}